From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 14:03:27 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] tt_fpga: add macOS and Windows support for serial port
 and auto-detection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The TT MicroPython support was previously Linux-only (POSIX termios,
sysfs). This adds cross-platform support for all three platforms that
openFPGALoader targets:

Serial port:
- Linux/macOS: POSIX termios (shared, both support the same API)
- Windows: Win32 CreateFile/ReadFile/WriteFile with DCB configuration

Auto-detection:
- Linux: scan /sys/class/tty/ttyACM* + sysfs idVendor/idProduct
- macOS: scan /dev/cu.usbmodem* (VID/PID filtering requires -d for
  disambiguation when multiple USB modem devices are present)
- Windows: SetupDi enumeration with VID/PID from hardware ID string,
  COM port name from registry

Other changes:
- Replace usleep() with cross-platform sleep_ms() helper
- Use int return type for serialRead/serialWrite (portable)
- Platform-specific handle: HANDLE on Windows, int fd on POSIX
- Link setupapi.lib on Windows for SetupDi functions
- Remove Linux-only cmake guard (now builds on all platforms)

Tested on Linux (pi27 aarch64) with GPIO loopback — 20/20 PASS.
macOS and Windows builds are compile-tested only (no hardware).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
